  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our expression and mark the occurrences of the variables as bound $(\\text{b})$ or free $(\\text{f}).$\n\n- Occurrence I of the variable $y$ is *bound* since it's placed right next to the quantifier $\u2200:$\n\n$$\n\u2200{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+x\\le z\n$$\n\n- Occurrence II of the variable $x$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $x.$\n\n- Occurrence III of the variable $z$ is *free* since it isn't placed right next to a quantifier and it doesn't lie within the scope of a quantifier that uses $z.$\n\nThe occurrences of variables in the expression are as follows:\n\n$$\n\u2200{y}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{b}\\end{aligned}}\\in Z,\\,y+{x}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\\le {z}_{\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \u2191 \\\\ \\text{f}\\end{aligned}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the free occurrences are \"II and III only.\"",
